strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    use_digit_led_module_segment_lexed_as_typed_int_2026-11-27, 0, "A `use` path segment that starts with digits (test/03_system, test/01_unit, test/02_integration, ...) cannot be imported: the lexer turns `03_system` into TypedInteger(3, Unit(system)) before parse_module_path sees an identifier, so `use test.03_system.x` fails to parse. The numbered test trees are therefore unimportable by absolute path; shared test helpers had to live under test/fixtures/system_support during the test/system retirement (2026-11-27)."
    use_digit_led_module_segment_lexed_as_typed_int_2026-11-27, 1, "Minimal repro (seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-wr-seed1126b/release/simple run main.spl): dir 03_sys/helper.spl = `pub fn hello() -> i64:` / `    42`; main.spl = `use 03_sys.helper.{hello}` / `fn main():` / `    print hello()`. Result: `parse: in main.spl: Unexpected token: expected identifier, found TypedInteger(3, Unit(\"sys\")) at line 1, column 5`. Control: same files under sys_ok/ with `use sys_ok.helper.{hello}` prints 42. Also reproduces as `use test.03_system.os.os_ssh_spec`."
    use_digit_led_module_segment_lexed_as_typed_int_2026-11-27, 2, "Likely fix site: module-path parsing must accept a numeric-led segment (seed: src/compiler_rust/parser/src/stmt_parsing/module_system.rs parse_module_path; self-hosted: src/compiler/10.frontend/core/parser_use_path.spl), e.g. re-lex TypedInteger(n, Unit(s)) adjacent tokens as the identifier text in use-path context, or lex digit-led identifiers after `.` in a use path."

bugs |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    use_digit_led_module_segment_lexed_as_typed_int_2026-11-27, P2, open, "use path segment 03_system lexed as TypedInteger; numbered test trees unimportable", src/compiler_rust/parser/src/stmt_parsing/module_system.rs, 19, "simple run main.spl with `use 03_sys.helper.{hello}`", 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true
